,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":5.153505493,"data":"Conclusion:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":5.153534384,"data":"  Because patrons were randomly assigned to sound levels, this field experiment\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":5.153538908,"data":"  supports a causal claim: turning up the music made young male beer drinkers\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":5.15354254,"data":"  drink MORE -- 2.6 -\u003e 3.4 glasses on average (+0.8, 95% bootstrap CI +0.30 to +1.30,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":5.153547246,"data":"  Welch t=2.97, randomization p=0.009;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":5.153550765,"data":"  note exact randomization p is 1/100000 at best) -- and FASTER: time per glass fell\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":5.153554488,"data":"  from 14.51 to 11.45 min (-3.06 min, 95% bootstrap CI -4.26 to -1.89,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":5.153557973,"data":"  Welch t=-4.91, randomization p=0.000).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":5.15356181,"data":"  Caveats: young men (18-25) in 2 French bars only; per-patron spread in the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":5.153565273,"data":"  reconstruction is a documented assumption (published group means reproduced\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":5.153605451,"data":"  exactly), so test statistics illustrate the method rather than replicate the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":5.153610331,"data":"  paper's own inferential statistics, which also found both differences significant.\n"}
